    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has many unused imports, unused constants, and long dense method chains. I'll write an improved version that's cleaner and easier to understand.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports, unused constants (`UTF_16`, `UTF_8`, `TEST_STRING`, `LARGE_TEST_STRING`), and the unused `random` field, introduces a named `nullCharsetName` variable to make the intent explicit, extracts `defaultCharset` and `bufferSize` into named variables shared between both test paths, and reformats the builder chain for readability — while preserving the exact same method calls, arguments, and assertions as the original."
